<title>DUBAI: HORSE RACING-DUBAI WORLD CUP RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-DUBAI WORLD CUP RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Dubai World Cup horse</p>
<p>race for four-year-olds and upwards, run over one mile and a</p>
<p>quarter (2-km) on Thursday (London betting odds): 1. Singspiel</p>
<p>13-2 (ridden by Jerry Bailey)</p>
<p>2. Siphon 11-4 favourite (David Flores)</p>
<p>3. Sandpit 7-2 (Corey Nakatani)</p>
<p>12 ran. Helissio was a non-runner</p>
<p>Distances: 1 1/4 lenghts, 1 1/2</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed and trained in England by</p>
<p>Michael Stoute</p>
<p>Value to wining owner: 1,428,571 sterling (2.4 million</p>
<p>dollars).</p>
</text>
